\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11min_voting_period\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dexecute_delay\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cactivates_at\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\19ConflictOfInterestUpdated\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\1cconflict_of_interest_updated\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07changed\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\d1Veto a proposal.\0a\0aAny maintainer can veto an active proposal, during the vote and the\0aexecute delay, whatever the votes are. A veto only rejects: the\0aproposal becomes `Vetoed`, runs no outcome call and cannot be executed\0aor voted on. Unlike [`DaoTrait::revoke_proposal`], which deletes spam\0aand forfeits the deposit, the proposal stays readable and the\0aproposer's deposit is repaid; who vetoed, why and when stay readable with\0a[`DaoTrait::get_veto`]. It needs no tally, so it also ends an\0aanonymous proposal whose ballots cannot be tallied.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - The maintainer vetoing the proposal\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal to veto\0a* `reason` - IPFS content identifier of the explanation, stored and published in the event\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If the proposal is not active\0a* If the reason is not an IPFS content identifier of 32 to 64 characters\00\00\00\00\00\00\04veto\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06reason\00\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\cdCast a vote on a proposal.\0a\0aAllows a member to vote on a proposal.\0aThe vote can be either public or anonymous depending on the proposal configuration.\0aFor public votes, the choice and weight are visible. For anonymous votes, only\0athe weight is visible, and the choice is encrypted.\0a\0aBadge-based proposals cap weight by membership badges. Token-based\0aproposals require `weight` (whole tokens) not to exceed the voter's\0acurrent token balance. Votes of weight 1 take at most\0a`MAX_DEFAULT_WEIGHT_VOTES` of the `MAX_VOTES_PER_PROPOSAL` slots.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `voter` - The address of the voter\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal to vote on\0a* `vote` - The vote data (public or anonymous)\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the voter has already voted\0a* If the voting period has ended\0a* If the proposal is not active anymore\0a* If the proposal doesn't exist\0a* If the voter's weight exceeds their maximum allowed weight\00\00\00\00\00\00\04vote\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05voter\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04vote\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\04Vote\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Verify vote commitment proof for anonymous voting.\0a\0aValidates that the provided tallies and seeds match the vote commitments\0awithout revealing individual votes. This ensures the integrity of anonymous\0avoting results.\0a\0aThe commitment is:\0a\0aC = g^v * h^r (in additive notation: g*v + h*r),\0a\0awhere g, h are BLS12-381 generator points and v is the vote choice,\0ar is the seed. Voting weight is introduced during the tallying phase.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal` - The proposal containing vote commitments\0a* `tallies` - Decoded tally values [approve, reject, abstain] (scaled by weights)\0a* `seeds` - Decoded seed values [approve, reject, abstain] (scaled by weights, modulo the group order)\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `bool` - True if all commitments match the provided tallies and seeds\0a\0aOnly `proposal.id` is used; the proposal is read from storage.\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If no anonymous voting configuration exists for the project\0a* If the proposal doesn't exist\0a* If `tallies` \00\00\00\05proof\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08proposal\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\08Proposal\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07tallies\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05seeds\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0c\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Execute a vote after the voting period ends.\0a\0aProcesses the voting results and determines the final status of the proposal.\0aFor public votes, the results are calculated directly from vote counts.\0aFor anonymous votes, tallies and seeds are validated against vote commitments\0ato ensure the results are correct.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - The address of the maintainer executing the proposal\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal to execute\0a* [`Option<tallies>`] - decoded tally values (scaled by weights), respectively Approve, reject and abstain\0a* [`Option<seeds>`] - decoded seed values (scaled by weights, modulo the group order), respectively Approve, reject and abstain\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::ProposalStatus` - The final status of the proposal (Approved, Rejected, or Cancelled)\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the voting period hasn't ended\0a* If the proposal doesn't exist\0a* If the proposal is not active anymore\0a* If tallies/seeds are missing for anonymo\00\00\00\07execute\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07tallies\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05seeds\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0c\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eProposalStatus\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\ebReturns a page of proposals (0 to MAX_PROPOSALS_PER_PAGE proposals per page).\0a\0aProposal `id` is on page `id / MAX_PROPOSALS_PER_PAGE`. Revoked\0aproposals are deleted and left out, so a page can hold fewer, and a\0apage past the last proposal is empty.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `page` - The page number (0-based)\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::Dao` - The DAO object containing a page of proposals\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the project doesn't exist\00\00\00\00\07get_dao\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04page\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\03Dao\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\013Get who vetoed a proposal, why and when.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::Veto` - The maintainer, the CID of the reason and the ledger timestamp\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the proposal was not vetoed\00\00\00\00\08get_veto\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\04Veto\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\aaRemove a malicious or non-compliant vote from a proposal.\0a\0aOnly a project maintainer can call this. The vote and its tally\0acontribution are dropped. The vote must be cast on an active proposal\0a(removal is allowed even after the voting period ends) and its ballot\0amust still live: see [`DaoTrait::vote`].\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - Address of the maintainer removing the vote\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal\0a* `voter` - The address of the voter whose vote is being removed\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If the proposal is not active\0a* If no vote from the given voter exists\00\00\00\00\00\0bremove_vote\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05voter\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01TGet a single proposal by ID.\0a\0a`vote_data.votes` lists the ballots that have not expired (see `vote`).\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal to retrieve\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::Proposal` - The proposal object\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the proposal doesn't exist\00\00\00\0cget_proposal\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\08Proposal\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Create a new proposal for a project.\0a\0aThe proposer is automatically added to the abstain group.\0aBy creating a proposal, the proposer incur a collateral which is\0arepaid upon execution of the proposal unless the proposal is revoked.\0aThis is a deterrent mechanism.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `proposer` - Address of the proposal creator\0a* `project_key` - Unique identifier for the project\0a* `title` - Title of the proposal\0a* `ipfs` - IPFS content identifier describing the proposal\0a* `voting_ends_at` - UNIX timestamp when voting ends\0a* `public_voting` - Whether voting is public or anonymous\0a* [`Option<token_contract>`] - token contract for token-based voting;\0aonly a maintainer sets one, and never on a project weighted by NQG\0a* [`Option<Vec<OutcomeContract>>`] - at most three outcome contracts,\0afor Approved, Rejected and Cancelled, run by the executor\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `u32` - The ID of the created proposal.\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the title is too long\0a* If the voting period is invalid\0a* If the project doesn't\00\00\00\0fcreate_proposal\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08proposer\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05title\00\00\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04ipfs\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0evoting_ends_at\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dpublic_voting\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0etoken_contract\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11outcome_contracts\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0fOutcomeContract\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\e2Revoke a proposal.\0a\0aUseful if there was some spam or bad intent. Deletes the proposal; its\0aid stays taken and its ballots expire on their own. Forfeits the\0aproposer's collateral.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - Address of the maintainer or admin revoking the proposal\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal to revoke\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the proposal is not active anymore\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\00\00\00\00\00\0frevoke_proposal\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\9fSetup anonymous voting for a project.\0a\0aConfigures BLS12-381 cryptographic primitives for anonymous voting.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - The address of the maintainer (must be authorized)\0a* `project_key` - Unique identifier for the project\0a* `public_key` - Asymmetric public key to be used for vote encryption\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the caller is not an authorized maintainer of the project\00\00\00\00\16anonymous_voting_setup\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0apublic_key\00\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\c2Add addresses to the conflict-of-interest list of a proposal.\0a\0aAddresses on the list cannot cast a vote on the proposal.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - A maintainer of the project (must authenticate)\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal\0a* `addresses` - Addresses to add to the list\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If the proposal is not active anymore\00\00\00\00\00\18add_conflict_of_interest\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09addresses\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00Get the conflict-of-interest list for a proposal.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `Vec<Address>` - Addresses barred from voting on the proposal\00\00\00\18get_conflict_of_interest\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\01'Get the anonymous voting configuration for a project.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::AnonymousVoteConfig` - The anonymous voting configuration\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If no anonymous voting configuration exists for the project\00\00\00\00\1bget_anonymous_voting_config\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\13AnonymousVoteConfig\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\91Remove addresses from the conflict-of-interest list of a proposal.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - A maintainer of the project (must authenticate)\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `proposal_id` - The ID of the proposal\0a* `addresses` - Addresses to remove from the list\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If the proposal is not active anymore\00\00\00\00\00\00\1bremove_conflict_of_interest\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproposal_id\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09addresses\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03hBuild vote commitments from votes and seeds for anonymous voting.\0a\0aCreates BLS12-381 commitments for each vote using the formula:\0aC = g\c2\b7vote + h\c2\b7seed where g and h are generator points on BLS12-381.\0a\0aNote: This function does not consider voting weights, which are applied\0aduring the tallying phase. Calling this on the smart contract would reveal\0athe votes and seeds, and so does a simulation to the RPC server that runs\0ait: a voter computes them client-side, this function is the reference.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - Unique identifier for the project\0a* `votes` - Vector of vote choices (0=approve, 1=reject, 2=abstain)\0a* `seeds` - A random scalar for each vote, modulo the group order\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `Vec<BytesN<96>>` - Vector of vote commitments (one per vote)\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If no anonymous voting configuration exists for the project\00\00\00\1cbuild_commitments_from_votes\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05votes\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0a\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05seeds\00\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0c\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00`\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\cdPause or unpause the contract (emergency stop.)\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `admin` - The admin address\0a* `paused` - Pause or unpause the contract operations which change\0aledger states.\00\00\00\00\00\00\05pause\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06paused\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00YGet the current version of the contract.\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `u32` - The contract version number\00\00\00\00\00\00\07version\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\efSet the contract running the outcome calls of proposals.\0a\0aThe executor has no upgrade: a new one is deployed and set here.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `admin` - The admin address\0a* `executor` - The new executor contract\00\00\00\00\0cset_executor\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08executor\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01CInitialize the Tansu contract with admin configuration.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `admin` - The admin address\0a* `collateral` - The Stellar asset contract deposits are paid in\0a* `executor` - The contract running the outcome calls of proposals\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If `collateral` is not a Stellar asset contract\00\00\00\00\0d__constructor\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0acollateral\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08executor\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\d5Approve an upgrade proposal\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `admin` - An admin address\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the admin is not authorized\0a* If the admin already approved\0a* If there is no upgrade to approve\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fapprove_upgrade\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01NPropose a contract upgrade.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `admin` - An admin address\0a* `new_wasm_hash` - The new WASM hash\0a* `new_admins_config` - Optional new admin configuration (None to keep current)\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the admin is not authorized\0a* If there is already an existing proposal (cancel the previous first)\00\00\00\00\00\0fpropose_upgrade\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dnew_wasm_hash\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11new_admins_config\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cAdminsConfig\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00Execute or cancel upgrade proposal\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `admin` - An admin address\0a* `accept` - true to accept and false to reject.\0a\0aUpgrades can always be cancelled but only executed if there are enough\0aapprovals and the timelock period is over.\0aNote that current governance rules apply. New config changes only\0ain force after an update.\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the admin is not authorized\0a* If it is too early to execute\0a* If there are not enough approvals\0a* If there is no upgrade to execute\00\00\00\10finalize_upgrade\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06accept\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\9dGet current administrators configuration.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::AdminsConfig` - The administrators configuration\00\00\00\00\00\00\11get_admins_config\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cAdminsConfig\00\00\00\00\00\00\00^Require that the contract is not paused, panic if it is\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the contract is paused.\00\00\00\00\00\12require_not_paused\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\1cGet upgrade proposal details\00\00\00\14get_upgrade_proposal\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0fUpgradeProposal\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\ccAdd a new member to the system with metadata.\0a\0aOptionally binds a Git identity. When provided, the identity is verified\0aby checking an Ed25519 signature against the caller's address, public key,\0aand identity string. Only `git_identity` and `git_pubkey` are persisted.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `member_address` - The address of the member to add\0a* `meta` - Metadata string associated with the member (e.g., IPFS hash)\0a* `git_identity` - Git handle (e.g., \22github:alice\22)\0a* `git_pubkey` - Ed25519 public key\0a* `git_sig` - Ed25519 signature\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the member already exists\0a* If git params are incomplete (identity, key, sig must be all Some or None)\0a* If the signature verification fails\00\00\00\0aadd_member\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0emember_address\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04meta\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cgit_identity\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0agit_pubkey\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07git_sig\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00@\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01eGet all badges for a specific project, organized by badge type.\0a\0aReturns a structure containing vectors of member addresses for each badge type\0a(Developer, Triage, Community, Verified).\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `key` - The project key identifier\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::Badges` - Structure containing member addresses for each badge type\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aget_badges\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06Badges\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\1dGet member information including all project badges.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `member_address` - The address of the member to retrieve\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::Member` - Member information including metadata and project badges\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the member doesn't exist\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aget_member\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0emember_address\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\06Member\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03)Set badges for a member in a specific project.\0a\0aThis function replaces all existing badges for the member in the specified project\0awith the new badge list. Repeated badges count once, and an empty list\0aremoves the project from the member's record. The member's maximum\0avoting weight is calculated as the sum of all assigned badge weights.\0aA member can remove a project from its own record, never add one.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - A maintainer of the project, or the member itself with an empty list\0a* `key` - The project key identifier\0a* `member` - The address of the member to set badges for\0a* `badges` - Vector of badges to assign\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If the member doesn't exist\0a* If the project doesn't exist\0a* If `badges` holds `Default`\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aset_badges\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06member\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06badges\00\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\05Badge\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02aUpdate the metadata and optionally the Git identity of an existing member.\0a\0aWhen `git_identity` is `Some`, the signature is verified the same way\0aas in `add_member` to prevent identity impersonation.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `member_address` - The address of the member to update\0a* `meta` - New metadata string\0a* `git_identity` - Git handle (e.g., \22github:alice\22)\0a* `git_pubkey` - Ed25519 public key\0a* `git_sig` - Ed25519 signature\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the member doesn't exist\0a* If git params are incomplete (identity, key, sig must be all Some or None)\0a* If the signature verification fails\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dupdate_member\00\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0emember_address\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04meta\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cgit_identity\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0agit_pubkey\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07git_sig\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00@\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02.Get the maximum voting weight for an address in a specific project.\0a\0aCalculates the sum of all badge weights for the address in the project.\0aReturns the Default badge weight (1) if the address has no badges\0aassigned or is not a registered member.\0a\0aA project with an NQG contract set (see `set_nqg_contract`) uses the\0aweight that contract gives instead of badges.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `member_address` - The address to check\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `u32` - The maximum voting weight for the address\00\00\00\00\00\0eget_max_weight\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0emember_address\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00*Get the NQG contract of a project, if any.\00\00\00\00\00\10get_nqg_contract\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bContractRef\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02NSet, or clear, the NQG contract giving the voting weights of a project.\0a\0aWhen set, `get_max_weight` returns the contract's\0a`get_voting_power(user: Address) -> u32` for the project, and badges\0aare not used. A weight of 0 means the address cannot vote. A call that\0afails reads as 0.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - A maintainer of the project\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `nqg_contract` - The NQG contract, or `None` to use badges again\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If the contract's WASM hash does not match the given one\00\00\00\00\00\10set_nqg_contract\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cnqg_contract\00\00\03\e8\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bContractRef\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Record an endorsement (attestation) of a commit or evidence artifact.\0a\0aA multi-party primitive: independent maintainers vouch that they verified the\0atarget. Each maintainer may attest a given target at most once \e2\80\94 a second\0acall from the same attester is rejected rather than replacing the first, so\0aan attestation is never silently rewritten. Revoking one is an explicit,\0aseparately evented action: see `revoke_attestation`. At most\0a`MAX_ATTESTATIONS` are kept on-chain; at capacity, vouches from addresses\0athat are no longer maintainers are pruned, and the call is rejected if\0athat does not free a slot. Current maintainers' vouches are never evicted.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `attester` - The maintainer recording the attestation\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `commit_hash` - The commit hash being endorsed\0a* `target` - The attestation target: the commit or a specific evidence artifact\0a* `note` - Optional pointer (e.g. a reproducibility report CID)\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the contract i\00\00\00\06attest\00\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08attester\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bcommit_hash\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06target\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\11AttestationTarget\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04note\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\bfSet the latest commit hash for a project.\0a\0aUpdates the current commit hash for the specified project.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - The address of the maintainer calling this function\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `hash` - The new commit hash\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the project doesn't exist\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If the hash is not a valid SHA-1 (40 hex) or SHA-256 (64 hex) object name\00\00\00\00\06commit\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04hash\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Register a new project.\0a\0aCreates a new project entry with maintainers, URL, and metadata.\0aThe project key is generated using keccak256 hash of the project name.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - The address of the maintainer calling this function\0a* `name` - The project name, 4 to 30 letters and digits\0a* `maintainers` - List of maintainer addresses for the project\0a* `url` - The project's Git repository URL\0a* `ipfs` - CID of the tansu.toml file with associated metadata\0a* `min_voting_period` - Optional minimum voting period override, in seconds\0a* `execute_delay` - Optional DAO execute timelock override, in seconds\0a* `attestation_threshold` - Optional finality threshold percent; when\0a`None` the project is set to `DEFAULT_FINALITY_THRESHOLD_PERCENT`. Can\0abe changed later with `set_attestation_threshold`.\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `Bytes` - The project key (keccak256 hash of the name)\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the project name is not 4 to 30 letters and digits\0a* If `url` or `ipfs` is longer than 256 bytes\0a* If\00\00\00\08register\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04name\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bmaintainers\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03url\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04ipfs\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11min_voting_period\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dexecute_delay\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\15attestation_threshold\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\ddGet the latest commit hash for a project.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `String` - The current commit hash\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the project doesn't exist\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aget_commit\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\01 Get project information including configuration and maintainers.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::Project` - Project information including name, config, and maintainers\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the project doesn't exist\00\00\00\0bget_project\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07Project\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02NGet the stored evidence history for a specific project commit and kind.\0a\0aEntries are returned oldest-first (the last element is the latest), and at\0amost `MAX_EVIDENCE` are kept on-chain. Returns an empty vector when no\0aevidence has been recorded; consumers reconstruct the full history from\0a`EvidenceSet` events via an indexer.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `commit_hash` - The commit hash this evidence describes\0a* `kind` - The evidence category\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `Vec<types::Evidence>` - The stored evidence pointers, oldest-first\00\00\00\00\00\0cget_evidence\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bcommit_hash\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04kind\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cEvidenceKind\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\08Evidence\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\b6Get a page of projects.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `page` - The page number (0-based)\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `Vec<types::Project>` - List of projects on the requested page\00\00\00\00\00\0cget_projects\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04page\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\07Project\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\deStore generic external evidence for a specific project commit and evidence kind.\0a\0aStores only the verifiable IPFS pointer. Evidence contents remain off-chain.\0a\0aEvidence is append-only: each call adds a new entry to the history for\0a`(project_key, commit_hash, kind)` rather than overwriting the previous\0aone (e.g. successive CVE re-scans of the same commit). At most\0a`MAX_EVIDENCE` entries are kept on-chain; older ones roll off but remain\0arecoverable from `EvidenceSet` events via an indexer.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - The address of the maintainer calling this function\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `commit_hash` - The commit hash this evidence describes\0a* `kind` - The evidence category\0a* `cid` - The off-chain content identifier\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the contract is paused\0a* If the project doesn't exist\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If commit_hash is not a valid SHA-1 (40 hex) or SHA-256 (64 hex) object name\0a* If cid is empty\00\00\00\00\00\0cset_evidence\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bcommit_hash\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04kind\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0cEvidenceKind\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03cid\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Update the configuration of an existing project.\0a\0aChanges the project's URL, IPFS metadata, and maintainer list, and\0aoptionally its governance overrides. `None` governance params leave\0athe current values untouched; to restore a default, pass it explicitly.\0a\0aTightening (new >= current) applies immediately; loosening activates\0aafter a notice window of current `min_voting_period + execute_delay`.\0aIn-flight proposals keep their creation-time timelock.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - The address of the maintainer calling this function\0a* `key` - The project key identifier\0a* `maintainers` - New list of maintainer addresses\0a* `url` - New Git repository URL\0a* `ipfs` - New CID of the tansu.toml file with metadata\0a* `min_voting_period` - Optional new minimum voting period, in seconds\0a* `execute_delay` - Optional new DAO execute timelock, in seconds\0a* `attestation_threshold` - Optional new finality threshold percent;\0awhen `None` the project's current threshold is left unchanged\0a\0a# Panics\0a* \00\00\00\0dupdate_config\00\00\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bmaintainers\00\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03url\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04ipfs\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11min_voting_period\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dexecute_delay\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\15attestation_threshold\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\a0Get the attestations recorded for a project's commit or evidence target.\0a\0aEntries are returned oldest-first (the last element is the most recent) and\0ahold at most one entry per attester, capped at `MAX_ATTESTATIONS`. The full\0ahistory stays recoverable from `Attested` events via an indexer.\0aReturns an empty vector when nothing has been attested for the target.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `commit_hash` - The commit hash the attestations relate to\0a* `target` - The attestation target: the commit or a specific evidence artifact\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `Vec<types::Attestation>` - The stored attestations, oldest-first\00\00\00\10get_attestations\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bcommit_hash\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06target\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\11AttestationTarget\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0bAttestation\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\e7Get sub-projects for a project (if it's an organization).\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `Vec<Bytes>` - List of sub-project keys, empty if not an organization\00\00\00\00\10get_sub_projects\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\02~Set sub-projects for a project (making it an organization).\0a\0aNote: by design, sub-project keys are not validated against existing\0aprojects. This allows reserving a project space before the project is\0aregistered (since the key is derived from the name). A project can\0aalso appear in multiple organizations.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - The maintainer address calling this function\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `sub_projects` - List of sub-project keys to associate\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the project doesn't exist\0a* If the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If more than 10 sub-projects are provided\00\00\00\00\00\10set_sub_projects\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0csub_projects\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Revoke the caller's own attestation from a target.\0a\0aOnly the attester can remove their vouch, and only their own: a maintainer\0acannot strike another's. Revocation is bounded twice over, so a vouch that\0aothers have already relied on cannot be pulled out from under them:\0a\0a1. **Not once the target is final.** An `attest` that brings the target\0ato its threshold records finality, which is never cleared. A target\0acan also read as final without that record after maintainers are\0aremoved; it then becomes revocable again if they are added back.\0a2. **Not after `ATTESTATION_REVOCATION_WINDOW`** has elapsed since\0a`created_at`. Past that the vouch is permanent.\0a\0aWithin those bounds, revoking frees the slot and the caller may attest the\0atarget again with a fresh `created_at` \e2\80\94 revoke plus re-attest is the\0asupported way to amend a `note` or correct a mistaken vouch. The\0a`Attested` / `AttestationRevoked` event pair is the durable audit trail.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `attester` - The maintainer revoki\00\00\00\12revoke_attestation\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08attester\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bcommit_hash\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06target\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\11AttestationTarget\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\22Compute whether an attestation target is final (canonical), on-chain.\0a\0aA target is final once the share of the project's *current* maintainers\0athat have attested it reaches the project's finality threshold. The target\0ais either the commit itself (`Commit`) or a specific evidence artifact\0a(`Evidence(kind, cid)`) tied to that commit. Attestations from addresses\0athat are no longer maintainers are ignored, so a removed maintainer's stale\0avouch cannot inflate the count.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `commit_hash` - The commit hash being evaluated\0a* `target` - The attestation target: the commit or a specific evidence artifact\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `types::FinalityStatus` - `{ attested, total, is_final }`\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the project doesn't exist\00\00\00\00\00\18get_attestation_finality\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bcommit_hash\00\00\00\00\10\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06target\00\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\11AttestationTarget\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0eFinalityStatus\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01QGet the attestation finality threshold (percent) for a project.\0a\0aReturns the project's stored threshold, or `DEFAULT_FINALITY_THRESHOLD_PERCENT`\0awhen the project has not set one.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a\0a# Returns\0a* `u32` - The finality threshold percent for the project\00\00\00\00\00\00\19get_attestation_threshold\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\036Set the attestation finality threshold (percent) for a project.\0a\0aA commit is considered final once the share of current maintainers that\0ahave attested it reaches this percentage. Every project defaults to\0a`DEFAULT_FINALITY_THRESHOLD_PERCENT` until its maintainers set a value here.\0aA higher threshold applies at once; a lower one after the notice window\0aof the project's `min_voting_period + execute_delay`.\0a\0a# Arguments\0a* `env` - The environment object\0a* `maintainer` - The address of the maintainer calling this function\0a* `project_key` - The project key identifier\0a* `percent` - The threshold percent (in `MIN_FINALITY_THRESHOLD_PERCENT..=100`)\0a\0a# Panics\0a* If the contract is paused\0a* If the project doesn't exist or the maintainer is not authorized\0a* If `percent` is below `MIN_FINALITY_THRESHOLD_PERCENT` or above 100\00\00\00\00\00\19set_attestation_threshold\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0amaintainer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bproject_key\00\00\00\00\0e\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\15attestation_threshold\00\00\00\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00")
)
